# PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER

The package ships this skill so an agent can drive the tool without reading
the source. It lives in the repo, versioned next to the code that it
documents; `just docs-sync` regenerates the CLI reference below from `--help`,
and `just check` fails when it is stale.

## Install

```bash
uv tool install git+https://github.com/OWNER_PLACEHOLDER/PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER@v0.1.0
```

Inside a clone, `uv run PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER ...` works without installing.

## Exit codes

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `0` | success |
| `1` | unexpected runtime error |
| `2` | usage error (bad flag or unknown subcommand) |
| `4` | validation error - the input was understood and rejected |

## Reading the output

`stdout` carries data; `stderr` carries logs and diagnostics. Pipe stdout
safely. `PROJECT_SLUG_PLACEHOLDER info` emits JSON on stdout and is the way to
find out what configuration the program actually resolved before blaming a
flag.

## Adding a subcommand

